From: Thomas Ritter <rittert@outlook.de>
Subject: [PATCH] gdiplus: Widen antialiased lines with the default flatness.

With a flatness of one pixel, antialiased curves visibly turn into
polygons.
---
diff --git a/dlls/gdiplus/graphics.c b/dlls/gdiplus/graphics.c
--- a/dlls/gdiplus/graphics.c
+++ b/dlls/gdiplus/graphics.c
@@ -4263,6 +4263,9 @@ static GpStatus SOFTWARE_GdipDrawPath(GpGraphics *graphics, GpPen *pen, GpPath *
             t.matrix[2] * t.matrix[2] + t.matrix[3] * t.matrix[3]));
     }
 
+    if (is_antialiased(graphics))
+        flatness *= FlatnessDefault;
+
     if (stat == Ok)
         stat = GdipWidenPath(wide_path, pen, transform, flatness);
 
